{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-array BFS. It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a wall border, marks visited cells as wall in a bytearray, and expands frontiers level by level. It prints the shortest S-to-E distance, or -1 if E is unreachable or S or E is missing. It matches all three public samples (in-0 got 2008, in-1 got -1, in-2 got 78, same as the expected outputs). A random 1000x1000 run with no path returned -1 in 0.2s. The assay registered a baseline median of 3.52091 with 1.4% noise. I stopped here rather than spend energy on a bidirectional or A* variant, since the gain would have to clear 3% to count.",
